import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'traps':('Surrounded by nobody',
  'Three walls carrying the trap flag and three trap-only floors around the Borg - and not one monster nearby. The surrounded check counted each trapped wall twice (once as a wall, once as a trap), pushing the safe-square count below zero, so "monsters greater than safe squares" fired with zero monsters: the original answers surrounded. The correction counts each non-safe grid once: not surrounded.'),
 'walls':('Control: eight plain walls',
  'Eight walls with no traps never touch the trap test: both variants answer not surrounded (zero monsters is never greater than zero safe squares), and the complete log is byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/surrounded-312 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag in ('RATING ','OUTCOME '):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[tag.split()[0].lower()]=match[1].strip() if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Surrounded by nobody</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native surrounded checks</p><h1>Surrounded by nobody</h1><p>The "am I about to be surrounded" check counted a trapped wall twice - once as a wall, once as a trap - so enough trapped neighbours pushed the safe-square count below zero and the verdict fired with no monsters nearby at all: the Borg abandoned fights and fled levels over a phantom.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the control establishes</h2><p>Eight plain walls never touch the trap test: both variants answer not surrounded, byte-identical logs. The correction changes only the trapped-wall double count.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior on an empty arena at depth 30, seed one thousand, with the eight neighbouring grids arranged as the report describes; the production borg_surrounded() verdict is read directly. The measured fact is the wrong verdict; the live in-game abandonment is the report's mechanism, not claimed here. No death or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/312">issue312</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);let r=d.rating||'';let m=r.match(/surrounded=(\\d)/);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=m?('Surrounded: '+(m[1]==='1'?'yes':'no')):'n/a';p.querySelector('.state').textContent=d.outcome||'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='traps'?'With zero monsters nearby the original answers surrounded - the double count drove safe squares negative; the correction answers no.':'Eight plain walls were never double-counted: not surrounded either way, byte for byte.';}select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
